IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-ch2-opting-in.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 2 -- Impediments to takeovers (ss 966 to 973).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- Seams (PLAN.md section 4): s 283 (special resolution, coa7), Schedule 1C (coa28), s 1121 (officer in default, coa24),
-- s 1173(1) (UK regulated market, the keel). Percentages are fractions of value compared by cross-multiplication (75% is 3 over 4).

§ `Part 28, Chapter 2: Impediments to takeovers`

§§ `Interpretation (s 971), used by the sections that follow`

-- s 971(1): "voting rights" and "voting shares".
-- src:13520 | “voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances;
@ref s 971(1)“voting rights” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13520-13520)
GIVEN `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the rights are voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including rights that arise only in certain circumstances
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question"

-- src:13521 | “voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights.
@ref s 971(1)“voting shares” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13521-13521)
GIVEN `the shares carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the shares are voting shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares carry voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting shares” means shares carrying voting rights"

-- s 971(1): "offeror" means the person making the bid.
-- src:13510 | “offeror”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the person making the bid;
@ref s 971(1)“offeror” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13510-13510)
GIVEN `the person is making the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the person is the offeror` MEANS
    IF `the person is making the takeover bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offeror”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the person making the bid"

-- s 971(1): "offer period" means the time allowed for acceptance of the bid by the rules made in accordance with paragraph 13 of Schedule 1C (a seam).
-- src:13511 | “offer period”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the time allowed for acceptance of the bid by—
@ref s 971(1)“offer period” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13511-13511)
GIVEN `sch 1C para 13 the day is within the time allowed for acceptance of the bid` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the day is within the offer period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1C para 13 the day is within the time allowed for acceptance of the bid`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offer period”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the time allowed for acceptance of the bid by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the time allowed is fixed by rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraph 13 of Schedule 1C

-- s 971(1): "takeover bid" has the meaning given by paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C (a seam).
-- src:13518 | “takeover bid” has the meaning given by paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C;
@ref s 971(1)“takeover bid” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13518-13518)
GIVEN `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the offer is a takeover bid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“takeover bid” has the meaning given by paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C is coa28's

-- s 971(2): securities and debentures treated as shares for the purposes of the Chapter.
-- src:13522 | (2) For the purposes of this Chapter—
-- src:13523 | (a) securities of a company are treated as shares in the company if they are convertible into or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares;
-- src:13524 | (b) debentures issued by a company are treated as shares in the company if they carry voting rights.
@ref s 971(2) Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13522-13524)
GIVEN `the securities are convertible into shares in the company or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities are debentures issued by the company that carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(2) the securities are treated as shares in the company` MEANS
    IF `the securities are convertible into shares in the company or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares` OR `the securities are debentures issued by the company that carry voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "securities of a company are treated as shares in the company if they are convertible into or entitle the holder to subscribe for such shares"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Opting in and opting out (ss 966 and 967)`

-- s 966(2): the first condition: voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
-- src:13421 | (2) The first condition is that the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
@ref s 966(2) Opting in and opting out (src:13421-13421)
GIVEN `the shares admitted to trading carry voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `s 971(1) the shares are voting shares` `the shares admitted to trading carry voting rights` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the company has voting shares admitted to trading on a UK regulated market."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "UK regulated market" is Article 2.1.13A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 (section 1173(1))

-- s 966(3): the second condition: no restrictions on the transfer of shares, or the articles disapply them (a) to transfers to the offeror and (b) to transfers when the offeror holds 75%.
-- src:13422 | (3) The second condition is that the company’s articles of association do not contain any restrictions on the transfer of shares or, if they do contain any such restrictions, provide that they are not to apply to—
-- src:13423 | (a) transfers to the offeror, or at the offeror’s direction to another person, during the offer period, or
-- src:13424 | (b) transfers to any person at a time during the offer period when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company.
@ref s 966(3) Opting in and opting out (src:13422-13424)
GIVEN `the articles contain restrictions on the transfer of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to the offeror, or at the offeror's direction to another person, during the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to any person during the offer period when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the articles contain restrictions on the transfer of shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       `they provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to the offeror, or at the offeror's direction to another person, during the offer period`
              AND `they provide that the restrictions do not apply to transfers to any person during the offer period when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that the company’s articles of association do not contain any restrictions on the transfer of shares or, if they do contain any such restrictions, provide that they are not to apply to"

-- s 966(3A): the third condition: no restrictions on voting rights, or they are disapplied at the two kinds of general meeting, unless compensated by specific pecuniary advantages.
-- src:13425 | (3A) The third condition is that the company’s articles of association—
-- src:13426 | (a) do not contain any restrictions on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company, or
-- src:13427 | (b) if they do contain any such restrictions, provide that they are not to have effect on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company that—
-- src:13428 | (i) decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid, or
-- src:13429 | (ii) is held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company,
-- src:13430 | unless the restrictions are compensated for by specific pecuniary advantages.
@ref s 966(3A) Opting in and opting out (src:13425-13430)
GIVEN `the articles contain restrictions on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide that the restrictions are not to have effect at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide that the restrictions are not to have effect at a general meeting held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restrictions are compensated for by specific pecuniary advantages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3A) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the articles contain restrictions on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the restrictions are compensated for by specific pecuniary advantages`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- the "unless the restrictions are compensated for by specific pecuniary advantages" limb: such restrictions need not be disapplied
         ELSE IF       `they provide that the restrictions are not to have effect at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid`
                   AND `they provide that the restrictions are not to have effect at a general meeting held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the company’s articles of association— (a) do not contain any restrictions on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company, or (b) if they do contain any such restrictions, provide that they are not to have effect"

-- s 966(3B) and (3C): the fourth condition: no other provision of the articles incompatible with requirements (a), (b) and (c).
-- src:13431 | (3B) The fourth condition is that the company’s articles of association do not contain any other provision which would be incompatible with the requirements of subsection (3C).
-- src:13432 | (3C) Those requirements are—
-- src:13433 | (a) multiple-vote shares are to carry only one vote each at a general meeting of the company that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid,
-- src:13434 | (b) multiple-vote shares are to carry only one vote each at a general meeting of the company which—
-- src:13435 | (i) is the first such meeting to be held after the end of the offer period,
-- src:13436 | (ii) is held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company, and
-- src:13437 | (iii) is called at the offeror’s request under section 969 in order to amend the company’s articles of association or to appoint or remove members of the board of directors, and
-- src:13438 | (c) at a time during the offer period when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company, shareholders are not to have any extraordinary rights to appoint or remove members of the board of directors.
@ref s 966(3B)-(3C) The fourth condition and its requirements (src:13431-13438)
GIVEN `an article is incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an article is incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at the first general meeting after the end of the offer period, held when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares and called at the offeror's request under section 969` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an article is incompatible with shareholders having no extraordinary rights to appoint or remove directors at a time during the offer period when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3B) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF       NOT (`an article is incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid`)
         AND NOT (`an article is incompatible with multiple-vote shares carrying only one vote each at the first general meeting after the end of the offer period, held when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares and called at the offeror's request under section 969`)
         AND NOT (`an article is incompatible with shareholders having no extraordinary rights to appoint or remove directors at a time during the offer period when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that the company’s articles of association do not contain any other provision which would be incompatible with the requirements of subsection (3C)."

-- s 966(3D): a reference to voting at a general meeting deciding on frustrating action includes voting on a written resolution on that question.
-- src:13439 | (3D) The references in subsections (3A)(b) and (3C)(a) to voting at a general meeting of the company that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid includes a reference to voting on a written resolution concerned with that question.
@ref s 966(3D) Opting in and opting out (src:13439-13439)
GIVEN `the vote is at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is on a written resolution concerned with that question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3D) the vote is within subsections (3A)(b) and (3C)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the vote is at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid` OR `the vote is on a written resolution concerned with that question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to voting on a written resolution concerned with that question"

-- s 966(3E): action which might result in the frustration of the bid is any action of that kind specified in rules (a seam: the rules and Schedule 1C).
-- src:13440 | (3E) For the purposes of subsections (3A)(b)(i) and (3C)(a), action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid is any action of that kind specified in rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraphs 17 or 18 of Schedule 1C.
@ref s 966(3E) Opting in and opting out (src:13440-13440)
GIVEN `sch 1C paras 17 and 18 the action is of a kind specified in rules under section 943(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3E) the action might result in the frustration of the takeover bid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1C paras 17 and 18 the action is of a kind specified in rules under section 943(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "action which might result in the frustration of the takeover bid is any action of that kind specified in rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraphs 17 or 18 of Schedule 1C"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rules and Schedule 1C paragraphs 17 and 18 are not among the sources

-- s 966(3F): references to voting shares in (3), (3A) and (3C) do not include debentures, or shares that do not normally carry rights to vote at general meetings.
-- src:13441 | (3F) The references in subsections (3), (3A) and (3C) to voting shares in the company do not include—
-- src:13442 | (a) debentures, or
-- src:13443 | (b) shares that, under the company’s articles of association, do not normally carry rights to vote at its general meetings (for example, shares carrying rights to vote that, under those articles, arise only where specified pecuniary advantages are not provided).
@ref s 966(3F) Opting in and opting out (src:13441-13443)
GIVEN `the thing is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3F) the thing is voting shares for subsections (3), (3A) and (3C)` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a debenture` OR `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The references in subsections (3), (3A) and (3C) to voting shares in the company do not include— (a) debentures, or (b) shares that"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what is not included, not what is

-- s 966(3G): "multiple-vote shares" means shares in a distinct and separate class carrying more than one vote each.
-- src:13444 | (3G) In subsection (3C), “multiple-vote shares” means shares included in a distinct and separate class and carrying more than one vote each.
@ref s 966(3G) Opting in and opting out (src:13444-13444)
GIVEN `the shares are included in a distinct and separate class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes each share carries` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(3G) the shares are multiple-vote shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are included in a distinct and separate class` AND `the votes each share carries` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“multiple-vote shares” means shares included in a distinct and separate class and carrying more than one vote each"

-- s 966(4): the fifth condition: no shares with special rights held by a minister, a nominee, or a company controlled by a minister, and no such rights exercisable by a minister under any enactment.
-- src:13445 | (4) The fifth condition is that—
-- src:13446 | (a) no shares conferring special rights in the company are held by—
-- src:13447 | (i) a minister,
-- src:13448 | (ii) a nominee of, or any other person acting on behalf of, a minister, or
-- src:13449 | (iii) a company directly or indirectly controlled by a minister,
-- src:13450 | and
-- src:13451 | (b) no such rights are exercisable by or on behalf of a minister under any enactment.
@ref s 966(4) Opting in and opting out (src:13445-13451)
GIVEN `shares conferring special rights in the company are held by a minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such shares are held by a nominee of, or another person acting on behalf of, a minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such shares are held by a company directly or indirectly controlled by a minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special rights in the company are exercisable by or on behalf of a minister under any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(4) the fifth condition is met` MEANS
    IF       NOT (`shares conferring special rights in the company are held by a minister`)
         AND NOT (`such shares are held by a nominee of, or another person acting on behalf of, a minister`)
         AND NOT (`such shares are held by a company directly or indirectly controlled by a minister`)
         AND NOT (`special rights in the company are exercisable by or on behalf of a minister under any enactment`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fifth condition is that— (a) no shares conferring special rights in the company are held by"

-- s 966(7): "minister" means the holders of office and bodies listed, and also includes the Treasury, the Board of Trade and the Defence Council.
DECLARE `s 966(7) body` IS ONE OF
    `s 966(7)(a) the holder of an office in Her Majesty's Government in the United Kingdom`
    `s 966(7)(b) the Scottish Ministers`
    `s 966(7)(c) a Minister within the meaning given by section 7(3) of the Northern Ireland Act 1998`
    `s 966(7)(d) the Welsh Ministers`
    `s 966(7) the Treasury`
    `s 966(7) the Board of Trade`
    `s 966(7) the Defence Council`
    `s 966(7) another body`

-- src:13454 | (7) In subsection (4) “minister” means—
-- src:13455 | (a) the holder of an office in Her Majesty's Government in the United Kingdom;
-- src:13456 | (b) the Scottish Ministers;
-- src:13457 | (c) a Minister within the meaning given by section 7(3) of the Northern Ireland Act 1998 (c. 47);
-- src:13458 | (d) the Welsh Ministers;
-- src:13459 | and for the purposes of that subsection “minister” also includes the Treasury, the Board of Trade and, the Defence Council . . . .
@ref s 966(7) Opting in and opting out (src:13454-13459)
GIVEN body IS A `s 966(7) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(7) the body is a minister for the purposes of subsection (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 966(7)(a) the holder of an office in Her Majesty's Government in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7)(b) the Scottish Ministers` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7)(c) a Minister within the meaning given by section 7(3) of the Northern Ireland Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7)(d) the Welsh Ministers` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7) the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7) the Board of Trade` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7) the Defence Council` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 966(7) another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In subsection (4) “minister” means—"

-- s 966(1): a company may by special resolution opt in if the five conditions are met. The special resolution is a seam (s 283, coa7).
-- src:13420 | (1) A company may by special resolution (an “opting-in resolution”) opt in for the purposes of this Chapter if the following five conditions are met in relation to the company.
@ref s 966(1) Opting in and opting out (src:13420-13420)
GIVEN `s 966(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(3A) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(3B) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(4) the fifth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(1) the company may opt in by the resolution` MEANS
    IF       `s 966(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         AND `s 966(3A) the third condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(3B) the fourth condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         AND `s 966(4) the fifth condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "A company may by special resolution ... opt in ... if the following five conditions are met"; a condition not met, or not known, or a resolution that is not special, is outside the grant, and the text does not say "may not" (fork F12)

-- s 966(1): "opting-in resolution" is the special resolution by which a company opts in.
-- src:13420 | (1) A company may by special resolution (an “opting-in resolution”) opt in for the purposes of this Chapter if the following five conditions are met in relation to the company.
@ref s 966(1) Opting in and opting out (src:13420-13420)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed to opt in for the purposes of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 966(1) the company may opt in by the resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(1) the resolution is an opting-in resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the resolution is passed to opt in for the purposes of Chapter 2`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by special resolution (an “opting-in resolution”) opt in for the purposes of this Chapter"
    ELSE `s 966(1) the company may opt in by the resolution`

-- s 966(5): a company may revoke an opting-in resolution by a further special resolution (an "opting-out resolution").
-- src:13452 | (5) A company may revoke an opting-in resolution by a further special resolution (an “opting-out resolution”).
@ref s 966(5) Opting in and opting out (src:13452-13452)
GIVEN `the company has passed an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the further resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(5) the company may revoke the opting-in resolution by the further resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed an opting-in resolution` AND `s 283 the further resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to revoke an opting-in resolution by a further special resolution"

-- src:13452 | (5) A company may revoke an opting-in resolution by a further special resolution (an “opting-out resolution”).
@ref s 966(5) Opting in and opting out (src:13452-13452)
GIVEN `the resolution is a further resolution passed to revoke an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 966(5) the resolution is an opting-out resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a further resolution passed to revoke an opting-in resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by a further special resolution (an “opting-out resolution”)"

-- s 967(1): an opting-in or opting-out resolution must specify the date from which it is to have effect.
-- src:13463 | (1) An opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution must specify the date from which it is to have effect (the “effective date”).
@ref s 967(1) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13463-13463)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies the date from which it is to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(1) the resolution specifies its effective date as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the resolution specifies the date from which it is to have effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution must specify the date from which it is to have effect (the “effective date”)."

-- s 967(1): the opting-in resolution has effect from its effective date until an opting-out resolution takes effect.
-- src:13463 | (1) An opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution must specify the date from which it is to have effect (the “effective date”).
@ref s 967(1) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13463-13463)
GIVEN `the effective date of the opting-in resolution` IS A DATE
      `the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(1) the opting-in resolution has effect on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` LESS THAN `the effective date of the opting-in resolution`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify the date from which it is to have effect"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST d THEN
             IF `the day` LESS THAN d
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may revoke an opting-in resolution by a further special resolution"

-- s 967(2): the effective date of an opting-in resolution may not be earlier than the date on which it is passed.
-- src:13464 | (2) The effective date of an opting-in resolution may not be earlier than the date on which the resolution is passed.
@ref s 967(2) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13464-13464)
GIVEN `the effective date of the opting-in resolution` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(2) the effective date of the opting-in resolution is permitted` MEANS
    IF `the effective date of the opting-in resolution` AT LEAST `the date on which the resolution is passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The effective date of an opting-in resolution may not be earlier than the date on which the resolution is passed."

-- s 967(3): the second to fifth conditions must be met when the opting-in resolution is passed; the first need not be met until the effective date.
-- src:13465 | (3) The second, third, fourth and fifth conditions in section 966 must be met at the time when an opting-in resolution is passed, but the first one does not need to be met until the effective date.
@ref s 967(3) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13465-13465)
GIVEN `s 966(3) the second condition was met when the resolution was passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(3A) the third condition was met when the resolution was passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(3B) the fourth condition was met when the resolution was passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(4) the fifth condition was met when the resolution was passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(2) the first condition is met on the effective date` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(3) the conditions are met at the times the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `s 966(3) the second condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 966(3A) the third condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          OR `s 966(3B) the fourth condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 966(4) the fifth condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          OR `s 966(2) the first condition is met on the effective date` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second, third, fourth and fifth conditions in section 966 must be met at the time when an opting-in resolution is passed, but the first one does not need to be met until the effective date."
    ELSE IF       `s 966(3) the second condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(3A) the third condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `s 966(3B) the fourth condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(4) the fifth condition was met when the resolution was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `s 966(2) the first condition is met on the effective date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- s 967(4): an opting-in resolution passed before admission to trading complies if it provides for effect from that time instead of a date.
-- src:13466 | (4) An opting-in resolution passed before the time when voting shares of the company are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market complies with the requirement in subsection (1) if, instead of specifying a particular date, it provides for the resolution to have effect from that time.
@ref s 967(4) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13466-13466)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies the date from which it is to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed before the voting shares were admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for the resolution to have effect from that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(4) the opting-in resolution complies with the requirement in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `s 967(1) the resolution specifies its effective date as the subsection requires` `the resolution specifies the date from which it is to have effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the resolution was passed before the voting shares were admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` AND `it provides for the resolution to have effect from that time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An opting-in resolution passed before the time when voting shares of the company are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market complies with the requirement in subsection (1) if, instead of specifying a particular date, it provides for the resolution to have effect from that time."

-- s 967(6): the effective date of an opting-out resolution may not be earlier than the first anniversary of the date a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar.
-- src:13468 | (6) The effective date of an opting-out resolution may not be earlier than the first anniversary of the date on which a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar.
@ref s 967(6) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13468-13468)
GIVEN `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` IS A DATE
      `the date on which a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(6) the effective date of the opting-out resolution is permitted` MEANS
    IF `the effective date of the opting-out resolution` AT LEAST (`add years` `the date on which a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar` 1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The effective date of an opting-out resolution may not be earlier than the first anniversary of the date on which a copy of the opting-in resolution was forwarded to the registrar."

-- s 967(7): an alteration of the articles that would prevent the second, third or fourth condition is of no effect until the effective date of an opting-out resolution.
-- src:13469 | (7) Where a company has passed an opting-in resolution, any alteration of its articles of association that would prevent the second, third or fourth condition in section 966 from being met is of no effect until the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company.
@ref s 967(7) Further provision about opting-in and opting-out resolutions (src:13469-13469)
GIVEN `the company has passed an opting-in resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration would prevent the second, third or fourth condition in section 966 from being met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 967(7) the alteration of the articles is still of no effect` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has passed an opting-in resolution` AND `the alteration would prevent the second, third or fourth condition in section 966 from being met`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on an alteration "that would prevent the second, third or fourth condition in section 966 from being met" by a company that "has passed an opting-in resolution"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST d THEN
             IF `the day` LESS THAN d
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is of no effect until the effective date of an opting-out resolution passed by the company"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Consequences of opting in (ss 968 and 969)`

-- s 968(1): the provisions have effect where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company.
-- src:13472 | (1) The following provisions have effect where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company.
@ref s 968(1) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13472-13472)
GIVEN `a takeover bid is made for the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 971(1) the company is an opted-in company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(1) the provisions have effect` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a takeover bid is made for the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following provisions have effect where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 971(1) the company is an opted-in company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following provisions have effect where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is an opted-in company is answered by section 971(1) from facts not given

-- s 971(1): "opted-in company" means a company in relation to which an opting-in resolution has effect and the conditions in section 966(2) and (4) continue to be met.
-- src:13513 | “opted-in company” means a company in relation to which—
@ref s 971(1)“opted-in company” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13513-13513)
GIVEN `an opting-in resolution has effect in relation to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(2) the first condition continues to be met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 966(4) the fifth condition continues to be met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the company is an opted-in company` MEANS
    IF `an opting-in resolution has effect in relation to the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 966(2) the first condition continues to be met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 966(4) the fifth condition continues to be met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“opted-in company” means a company in relation to which— (a) an opting-in resolution has effect, and (b) the conditions in section 966(2) and (4) continue to be met"
    ELSE IF `an opting-in resolution has effect in relation to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(2) the first condition continues to be met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 966(4) the fifth condition continues to be met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb's answer is not known

-- s 971(1): "opting-in resolution" and "opting-out resolution" have the meanings given by section 966(1) and (5).
-- src:13516 | “opting-in resolution” has the meaning given by section 966(1);
@ref s 971(1)“opting-in resolution” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13516-13516)
GIVEN `s 966(1) the resolution is an opting-in resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the resolution is an opting-in resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 966(1) the resolution is an opting-in resolution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“opting-in resolution” has the meaning given by section 966(1)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer is section 966(1)'s, which is not known

-- src:13517 | “opting-out resolution” has the meaning given by section 966(5);
@ref s 971(1)“opting-out resolution” Interpretation of this Chapter (src:13517-13517)
GIVEN `s 966(5) the resolution is an opting-out resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 971(1) the resolution is an opting-out resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 966(5) the resolution is an opting-out resolution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“opting-out resolution” has the meaning given by section 966(5)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer is section 966(5)'s, which is not known

-- s 968(3): the section applies to an agreement entered into between shareholders on or after 21 April 2004, or at any time between a shareholder and the company, even if the law applicable is not that of the United Kingdom.
-- src:13480 | (3) This section applies to an agreement—
-- src:13481 | (a) entered into between a person holding shares in the company and another such person on or after 21st April 2004, or
-- src:13482 | (b) entered into at any time between such a person and the company,
-- src:13483 | and it applies to such an agreement even if the law applicable to the agreement (apart from this section) is not the law of a part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 968(3) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13480-13483)
GIVEN `the agreement is between a person holding shares in the company and another such person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the agreement is between such a person and the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law applicable to the agreement is the law of a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(3) the section applies to the agreement` MEANS
    -- the answer does not depend on the applicable law: "it applies to such an agreement even if the law applicable to the agreement (apart from this section) is not the law of a part of the United Kingdom"
    IF (`the agreement is between a person holding shares in the company and another such person` AND `the date the agreement was entered into` AT LEAST (Date 21 4 2004)) OR `the agreement is between such a person and the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies to an agreement "(a) entered into between a person holding shares in the company and another such person on or after 21st April 2004, or (b) entered into at any time between such a person and the company"

-- s 968(2): an agreement to which the section applies is invalid in so far as it places a restriction of the four kinds.
DECLARE `s 968(2) restriction` IS ONE OF
    `s 968(2)(a) a restriction on the transfer to the offeror, or at his direction to another person, of shares during the offer period`
    `s 968(2)(b) a restriction on the transfer to any person of shares during the offer period when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares`
    `s 968(2)(c) a restriction on rights to vote at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid`
    `s 968(2)(d) a restriction on rights to vote at the first general meeting after the end of the offer period, held when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares`
    `s 968(2) another restriction`

-- src:13473 | (2) An agreement to which this section applies is invalid in so far as it places any restriction—
-- src:13474 | (a) on the transfer to the offeror, or at his direction to another person, of shares in the company during the offer period;
-- src:13475 | (b) on the transfer to any person of shares in the company at a time during the offer period when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company;
-- src:13476 | (c) on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid;
-- src:13477 | (d) on rights to vote at a general meeting of the company that—
-- src:13478 | (i) is the first such meeting to be held after the end of the offer period, and
-- src:13479 | (ii) is held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company.
@ref s 968(2) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13473-13479)
GIVEN `s 968(1) the provisions have effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 968(3) the section applies to the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      restriction IS A `s 968(2) restriction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(2) the agreement is invalid so far as it places the restriction` MEANS
    IF `s 968(1) the provisions have effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following provisions have effect where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company."
    ELSE IF `s 968(1) the provisions have effect` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 968(3) the section applies to the agreement` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the invalidity is of "An agreement to which this section applies", and whether it does is not shown
         ELSE CONSIDER restriction
              WHEN `s 968(2)(a) a restriction on the transfer to the offeror, or at his direction to another person, of shares during the offer period` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 968(2)(b) a restriction on the transfer to any person of shares during the offer period when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 968(2)(c) a restriction on rights to vote at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 968(2)(d) a restriction on rights to vote at the first general meeting after the end of the offer period, held when the offeror holds 75% in value of the voting shares` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 968(2) another restriction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the agreement is invalid "in so far as it places any restriction" of the four kinds (a) to (d)

-- s 968(4): the reference in (2)(c) to rights to vote at a general meeting deciding on frustrating action includes rights to vote on a written resolution concerned with that question.
-- src:13484 | (4) The reference in subsection (2)(c) to rights to vote at a general meeting of the company that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid includes a reference to rights to vote on a written resolution concerned with that question.
@ref s 968(4) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13484-13484)
GIVEN `the rights are rights to vote at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are rights to vote on a written resolution concerned with that question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(4) the rights are within subsection (2)(c)` MEANS
    IF `the rights are rights to vote at a general meeting that decides whether to take any action which might result in the frustration of the bid` OR `the rights are rights to vote on a written resolution concerned with that question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to rights to vote on a written resolution concerned with that question"

-- s 968(5): action which might result in the frustration of a bid is any action of that kind specified in rules made in accordance with paragraph 17 or 18 of Schedule 1C (a seam).
-- src:13485 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(c), action which might result in the frustration of a bid is any action of that kind specified in rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraph 17 or 18 of Schedule 1C.
@ref s 968(5) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13485-13485)
GIVEN `sch 1C paras 17 and 18 the action is of a kind specified in rules under section 943(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(5) the action might result in the frustration of the bid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1C paras 17 and 18 the action is of a kind specified in rules under section 943(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "action which might result in the frustration of a bid is any action of that kind specified in rules under section 943(1) made in accordance with paragraph 17 or 18 of Schedule 1C"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rules and Schedule 1C paragraphs 17 and 18 are not among the sources

-- s 968(6): compensation, of such amount as the court considers just and equitable, for loss from an act or omission that would but for this section be a breach of the agreement.
-- src:13486 | (6) If a person suffers loss as a result of any act or omission that would (but for this section) be a breach of an agreement to which this section applies, he is entitled to compensation, of such amount as the court considers just and equitable, from any person who would (but for this section) be liable to him for committing or inducing the breach.
@ref s 968(6) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13486-13486)
GIVEN `the person suffers loss as a result of an act or omission that would (but for this section) be a breach of an agreement to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person would (but for this section) be liable to him for committing or inducing the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the court considers just and equitable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 968(6) the compensation the person is entitled to` MEANS
    IF `the person suffers loss as a result of an act or omission that would (but for this section) be a breach of an agreement to which this section applies` AND `the other person would (but for this section) be liable to him for committing or inducing the breach`
    THEN JUST `the amount the court considers just and equitable`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is "from any person who would (but for this section) be liable to him for committing or inducing the breach"

-- s 968(7): "the court" is the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
DECLARE `s 968(7) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 968(7) the High Court`
    `s 968(7) the Court of Session`

-- src:13487 | (7) In subsection (6) “the court” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 968(7) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13487-13487)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 968(7) court`
`s 968(7) the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `s 968(7) the High Court`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN `s 968(7) the Court of Session`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 968(7) the High Court`

-- s 968(8) and s 969(2): references to voting shares do not include debentures, or shares that do not normally carry rights to vote at general meetings.
-- src:13488 | (8) A reference in this section to voting shares in the company does not include—
-- src:13489 | (a) debentures, or
-- src:13490 | (b) shares that, under the company's articles of association, do not normally carry rights to vote at its general meetings (for example, shares carrying rights to vote that, under those articles, arise only where specified pecuniary advantages are not provided).
@ref s 968(8) Effect on contractual restrictions (src:13488-13490)
GIVEN `the thing is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 968(8) the thing is voting shares for section 968` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a debenture` OR `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference in this section to voting shares in the company does not include— (a) debentures, or (b) shares that"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what is not included, not what is

-- src:13493 | (2) The reference in subsection (1) to voting shares in the company does not include—
-- src:13494 | (a) debentures, or
-- src:13495 | (b) shares that, under the company's articles of association, do not normally carry rights to vote at its general meetings (for example, shares carrying rights to vote that, under those articles, arise only where specified pecuniary advantages are not provided).
@ref s 969(2) Power of offeror to require general meeting to be called (src:13493-13495)
GIVEN `the thing is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 969(2) the thing is voting shares for subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a debenture` OR `the thing is shares that, under the articles, do not normally carry rights to vote at the company's general meetings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (1) to voting shares in the company does not include— (a) debentures, or (b) shares that"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what is not included, not what is

-- s 969(1): the offeror may by request require the directors to call a general meeting if he holds at least 75% in value of all the voting shares.
-- src:13492 | (1) Where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company, the offeror may by making a request to the directors of the company require them to call a general meeting of the company if, at the date at which the request is made, he holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company.
@ref s 969(1) Power of offeror to require general meeting to be called (src:13492-13492)
GIVEN `s 968(1) the provisions have effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of the shares the offeror holds at the date the request is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 969(1) the offeror may require the directors to call a general meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 968(1) the provisions have effect`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company, the offeror may by making a request to the directors of the company require them to call a general meeting of the company if"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the bid is made for an opted-in company is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the value of all the voting shares in the company` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the value of the shares the offeror holds at the date the request is made` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `the value of all the voting shares in the company` TIMES 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to require the directors to call a meeting "if, at the date at which the request is made, he holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company", and the text does not say "may not" (fork F13)

-- s 969(3): sections 303 to 305 apply as if subsection (1) were substituted for section 303(1) to (3) (a seam: coa7).
-- src:13496 | (3) Sections 303 to 305 (members' power to require general meetings to be called) apply as they would do if subsection (1) above were substituted for subsections (1) to (3) of section 303, and with any other necessary modifications.
@ref s 969(3) Power of offeror to require general meeting to be called (src:13496-13496)
GIVEN `s 969(1) the offeror may require the directors to call a general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 969(3) sections 303 to 305 apply to the request` MEANS
    IF `s 969(1) the offeror may require the directors to call a general meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sections 303 to 305 apply "as they would do if subsection (1) above were substituted for subsections (1) to (3) of section 303", for a request under subsection (1)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Supplementary (ss 970 to 972)`

-- s 970(1): a company that has passed an opting-in or opting-out resolution must notify the Panel.
-- src:13499 | (1) A company that has passed an opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution must notify—
-- src:13500 | (a) the Panel, ...
-- src:13501 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 970(1) Communication of decisions (src:13499-13501)
GIVEN `the company has passed an opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 970(1) the company must notify the Panel` MEANS
    IF `the company has passed an opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A company that has passed an opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution"

-- s 970(2): notification must be given within 15 days after the resolution is passed.
