@ref s 970(2) Communication of decisions (src:13502-13502)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 970(2) the last day for giving notification` MEANS `the day the resolution is passed` PLUS 15

-- src:13502 | (2) Notification must be given within 15 days after the resolution is passed ....
@ref s 970(2) Communication of decisions (src:13502-13502)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the day notification is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 970(2) the notification was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day notification is given` AT MOST (`s 970(2) the last day for giving notification` `the day the resolution is passed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notification must be given within 15 days after the resolution is passed"

-- s 970(1)-(2) as a regulative rule: the company must notify the Panel within 15 days (counted in days from the day the resolution is passed).
-- src:13499 | (1) A company that has passed an opting-in resolution or an opting-out resolution must notify—
-- src:13500 | (a) the Panel, ...
-- src:13501 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:13502 | (2) Notification must be given within 15 days after the resolution is passed ....
@ref s 970(1)-(2) Communication of decisions (src:13499-13502)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 970(1)-(2) the company's duty to notify the Panel` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, `Takeover Panel`, "notify the Panel of the opting-in or opting-out resolution"
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the Panel was not notified within 15 days after the resolution was passed"

-- s 970(3): if a company fails to comply, an offence is committed by the company and every officer of it who is in default.
DECLARE `s 970(3) who` IS ONE OF
    `s 970(3)(a) the company`
    `s 970(3)(b) an officer of the company`

-- src:13503 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:13504 | (a) the company, and
-- src:13505 | (b) every officer of it who is in default.
@ref s 970(3) Communication of decisions (src:13503-13505)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with section 970` IS A BOOLEAN
      who IS A `s 970(3) who`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 970(3) an offence is committed by` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company failed to comply with section 970`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER who
         WHEN `s 970(3)(a) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 970(3)(b) an officer of the company` THEN
             CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is by "every officer of it who is in default"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is section 1121's answer

-- s 970(4): the penalty: on summary conviction a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3.
-- src:13506 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 970(4) Communication of decisions (src:13506-13506)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 970(4) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives a penalty "on summary conviction" only

-- s 972(1): the transitory provisions apply where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company, until the repeal of sections 368 and 378 of the 1985 Act by this Act.
-- src:13526 | (1) Where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company, section 368 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (extraordinary general meeting on members' requisition) and section 378 of that Act (extraordinary and special resolutions) have effect as follows until their repeal by this Act.
@ref s 972(1) Transitory provision (src:13526-13526)
GIVEN `s 968(1) the provisions have effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sections 368 and 378 of the Companies Act 1985 have been repealed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` MEANS
    IF `sections 368 and 378 of the Companies Act 1985 have been repealed by this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "have effect as follows until their repeal by this Act"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 968(1) the provisions have effect`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a takeover bid is made for an opted-in company, section 368 of the Companies Act 1985"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the bid is made for an opted-in company is not known

-- s 972(2): section 368 has effect as if a members' requisition included a requisition of the offeror who holds at least 75% in value of all the voting shares at the date of the deposit.
-- src:13527 | (2) Section 368 has effect as if a members' requisition included a requisition of a person who—
-- src:13528 | (a) is the offeror in relation to the takeover bid, and
-- src:13529 | (b) holds at the date of the deposit of the requisition shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company.
@ref s 972(2) Transitory provision (src:13527-13529)
GIVEN `s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is the offeror in relation to the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the voting shares the person holds at the date of the deposit of the requisition` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 972(2) the requisition is treated as a members' requisition` MEANS
    IF `s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is the offeror in relation to the takeover bid` AND `the value of all the voting shares in the company` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the value of the voting shares the person holds at the date of the deposit of the requisition` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `the value of all the voting shares in the company` TIMES 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Section 368 has effect as if a members' requisition included a requisition of a person who"

-- s 972(3): for the first general meeting after the offer period, held while the offeror holds at least 75%, 14 days' notice for a special resolution instead of 21.
-- src:13530 | (3) In relation to a general meeting of the company that—
-- src:13531 | (a) is the first such meeting to be held after the end of the offer period, and
-- src:13532 | (b) is held at a time when the offeror holds shares amounting to not less than 75% in value of all the voting shares in the company,
-- src:13533 | section 378(2) (meaning of “special resolution”) has effect as if “14 days' notice” were substituted for “21 days' notice”.
@ref s 972(3) Transitory provision (src:13530-13533)
GIVEN `s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is the first general meeting of the company held after the end of the offer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the voting shares the offeror holds when the meeting is held` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 972(3) the days' notice for a special resolution` MEANS
    IF `s 972(1) the 1985 Act provisions have effect as the section provides` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the meeting is the first general meeting of the company held after the end of the offer period` AND `the value of all the voting shares in the company` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the value of the voting shares the offeror holds when the meeting is held` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `the value of all the voting shares in the company` TIMES 3
    THEN JUST 14
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the "21 days' notice" the 1985 Act's section 378(2) gives otherwise is not among the sources

-- s 972(4): references to voting shares do not include debentures, or shares that do not normally carry rights to vote.
